  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Consider an array BBB of size MMM.\n\nWe must perform the following operations with parameter i=1,2,…,M−1i = 1, 2, \\ldots, M - 1i=1,2,…,M−1 (in this order):\n\nNote that the order of operations is different than SUBSEQI.\n\n\nChoose an index jjj such that i&lt;j≤Mi \\lt j \\le Mi&lt;j≤M;\nReplace BjB_jBj​ in the array with max⁡(0,Bj−Bi)\\max(0, B_j - B_i)max(0,Bj​−Bi​).\n\nNote that the subsequent operations will be performed with the updated array BBB.\nAt the end of all operations, let f(B)f(B)f(B) denote the **maximum possible sum** of all elements of array BBB.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of size NNN.\n\nFind the sum of f(X)f(X)f(X) for all XXX which are non-empty subsequences of AAA. Note that there are exactly 2N−12^N - 12N−1 such XXX.\n\nSince the answer may be huge, output it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains one integer NNN, the size of the array AAA.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers, A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2,\\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the sum of f(X)f(X)f(X) over all 2N−12^N - 12N−1 subsequences of AAA, modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤4⋅1041 \\leq T \\leq 4 \\cdot 10^41≤T≤4⋅104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\le A_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
