        "input": "3\n3\n1 2 3\n4\n4 2 2 1\n6\n10 3 9 9 2 7",
        "output": "18\n57\n1052",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: It can be seen that :\n\nf([1])=1f([1]) = 1f([1])=1\nf([2])=2f([2]) = 2f([2])=2\nf([3])=3f([3]) = 3f([3])=3\nf([1,2])=2f([1, 2]) = 2f([1,2])=2\nf([2,3])=3f([2, 3]) = 3f([2,3])=3\nf([1,3])=3f([1, 3]) = 3f([1,3])=3\nf([1,2,3])=4f([1, 2, 3]) = 4f([1,2,3])=4 : You first choose j=2j = 2j=2 for operation with i=1i = 1i=1, and the new array is [1,1,3][1, 1, 3][1,1,3] and then you choose j=3j = 3j=3 for operation with i=2i = 2i=2, and the final array is [1,1,2][1, 1, 2][1,1,2]. Note that you subtracted the updated value of B2B_2B2​, i.e. 111 instead of the original 222.\n\nThus, the sum of f(X)f(X)f(X) over all non-empty subsequences of AAA equals 181818."
      }
